[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Source linking costs an export half a second warm and seven seconds cold

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-EXPORT-COST-WITH-LINKING
TITLE: Source linking costs an export half a second warm and seven seconds cold
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Source linking costs about +0.6 s on a warm export and about +7 s cold (9.3 s
vs 2.4 s cold, 2.8 s vs 2.1 s warm); `scribe check` is untaxed. The cost is in
the strictdoc export path with REQUIREMENT_TO_SOURCE_TRACEABILITY on. Two
candidates to measure first: the per-file mkdir under output/html/_source_files
that runs for every indexed file, and the NullSourceReader lookups for files no
extractor claims. `devenv tasks run strictdoc:bench` reproduces the numbers;
EV-STRICTDOC-EXPORT-TIMING records them.
<<<
